{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Nebuchadnezzar</b> — למכנש (to gather). To gather and assemble. <b>Satraps</b> and those mentioned after them — they are seven ranks in the Ishmaelite language, only we do not know the meaning of אדרגזריא and those that come after them. There was a sage in Sepharad who explained אדרגזריא as 'mighty ones of decrees,' but there is no need; therefore we leave them, for they are of no use." "<b>To</b> למתא (to come)."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra writes הם מעלות שבע בלשון ישמעאל; the reference is to the seven Aramaic administrative titles in Daniel 3:2–3, which he identifies via their cognates in Arabic."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:27.548746706Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}